      "side": 0,
      "message": "go/android.bp is the best reference I know, which says: \n\n- **apps_enabled** _bool_, If set to false, the ndk backend is exclusive to platform and is not available to applications. Default is true (i.e. available to both applications and platform).\n- **enabled** _bool_, Whether to generate code in the corresponding backend. Default:\n  - for Java/NDK/CPP backends - True\n  - for Rust backend - False\n  \nSo I _think_ we definitely want `enabled: true` so Rust code is emitted, but I\u0027m not sure about `apps_enabled`",
